the US Supreme Court stopped an  execution in Arkansas overnight just  minutes before the inmates death warrant  was set to expire Arkansas asked the  justices to remove illegal stay imposed  by a lower court on the execution of Don  Davis but the Supreme Court denied the  appeal in a one-sentence order Arkansas  had wanted to execute as many as seven  inmates by the end of this month  Omar Villafranca is outside the state  capital in Little Rock with now Arkansas  is now trying to resume capital  punishment for the first time in more  than a decade  Omar good morning good morning Don Davis  is on death row for the 1990 murder of  Jane Daniel when the Arkansas Supreme  Court stopped his execution the state  appealed to the US Supreme Court late  last night with minutes before his death  warrant expired the Supreme Court  weighed in about 15 minutes to midnight  the Supreme Court weighed in denying  Arkansas's appealed to let the execution  of convicted murderer Don Davis go  through we were told that he was in a  waiting cell late Monday night the state  was still preparing for Davis's  scheduled execution Bobby  Amazon with Arkansas public media was  picked to be in the room we were told  that the prison was fully staffed to  perform an execution at any moment Davis  was one of a group of seven men on death  row whose executions have been scheduled  over two weeks governor ASA Hutchinson  wants to carry them out before the  state's supply of midazolam one of the  controversial drugs used in the  execution process expires at the end of  the month the drug has been associated  with botched executions in four states  we are committed and working every  single minute to ensure again that  justice is carried out Arkansas Attorney  General Leslie Rutledge has made  numerous legal appeals there's a wrong  thing to do and there's a right thing to  do last week actor Johnny Depp joined  activists at a rally against the death  penalty these are people that I lived  with for 